<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/argentine-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Argentine%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Argentine Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Juan Perón is elected president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Italy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Italy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A referendum abolishes the monarchy and creates the Italian Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-indochina"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Indochina.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Indochina</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The First Indochina War begins after fighting in Haiphong and Hanoi</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-west-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20West%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French West Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The indigénat and forced labour are abolished and Africans become citizens</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/igbo-ukwu-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Igbo-Ukwu%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Igbo-Ukwu culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The district officer J. O. Field hands the objects he had bought to the Nigerian Department of Antiquities</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-austria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Austria.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Austria</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 26 July parliament passes the first nationalisation law; about 70 mining and manufacturing companies pass to the state.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/mandatory-palestine"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mandatory%20Palestine.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mandatory Palestine</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Irgun blows up the King David Hotel in Jerusalem, headquarters of the British administration, killing 92 people; Britain begins interning illegal Jewish immigrants in Cyprus.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/negritude"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/N%C3%A9gritude.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Négritude</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Léon Damas publishes the anthology Poètes d’expression française 1900–1945</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/republicanism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republicanism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republicanism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A referendum on 2 June makes Italy a republic, the first republican rule over the whole peninsula since ancient Rome</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/peronism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Peronism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Peronism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Perón is elected president of Argentina</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/dead-sea-scrolls"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dead%20Sea%20Scrolls.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dead Sea Scrolls</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Bedouin shepherds found the first seven scrolls in jars in what became Cave 1, between November 1946 and February 1947</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/democratic-republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Democratic%20Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Democratic Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The National Assembly adopts the first constitution in November, and in December the First Indochina War begins as the French reoccupy Hanoi</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1920-1946"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Hungary%20(1920-1946).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Hungary (1920-1946)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The monarchy is formally abolished on 1 February and replaced by the Second Hungarian Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/bhagavad-gita"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bhagavad%20Gita.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bhagavad Gita</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gandhi's commentary, written in Gujarati in 1929 and translated by Mahadev Desai, is published in English</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/fall-of-singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fall%20of%20Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fall of Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Yamashita is hanged in the Philippines after a war crimes trial that did not cover crimes in Malaya or Singapore</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/seoul"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Seoul.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Seoul</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The charter of the City of Seoul names the city Seoul and makes it a municipal corporation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/declaration-of-the-rights-of-man-and-of-the-citizen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Declaration%20of%20the%20Rights%20of%20Man%20and%20of%20the%20Citizen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The declaration is included at the beginning of the constitution of the Fourth Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/libertarianism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Libertarianism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Libertarianism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Leonard E. Read founds the Foundation for Economic Education</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/christian-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Christian%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Christian democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Popular Republican Movement becomes the largest party in the French parliament</span></li></ul></section>
